| `make test-sh` `[local]` | Runs every shell test file (`shell.test_suffixes`) with the runner `shell.test_runner` names, through `scripts/shell_gate.py`, after asking the runner to count the tests. It is a `make verify` goal of its own. | `make test-sh` | [`shell.enabled`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.excluded_paths`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.no_scripts`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.test_runner`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`shell.test_suffixes`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Exit 13 when shell scripts have no test file or the test files hold zero tests, because a pass over zero tests proves nothing; exit 11 when the runner is missing or gives no count. A project with no shell file is exit 13 unless `shell.no_scripts` states the reason, which it prints before it exits 0; `shell.enabled` false says so and exits 0. A file whose every test is skipped still counts and passes. Its counts are not in the evidence record. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
